        "original_id": "33dd8483-b787-5446-85cd-79ee9a2dc207",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dorothy Parker, Maxine Kumin, Barbara Swan, Anne Sexton, John Latouche, Lillian Hellman, Stephen Sondheim, John Mauceri, John Wells, Leonard Bernstein\n- Works: Candide (operetta)\n- Roles: Poet, author, short story writer, critic, satirist, contributor, collaborator\n\nFacts:\n- Dorothy Parker was born on August 22, 1893, and she was an American poet, short story writer, critic, and satirist known for her wit, wisecracks, and observations of 20th-century urban foibles.\n- Maxine Kumin was born on June 6, 1925, and she was an American poet and author.\n- Candide is an operetta whose text had additional contributors including John Latouche, Dorothy Parker, Lillian Hellman, Stephen Sondheim, John Mauceri, John Wells, and Leonard Bernstein.\n- Barbara Swan is known for collaborating with the poets Anne Sexton and Maxine Kumin.\n- Barbara Swan is also known for archived correspondence with various artists and writers.\n- Dorothy Parker died on June 7, 1967.\n- Maxine Kumin died on February 6, 2014.",
